@*
    Renders one antibiotic name together with the full name the pathologists
    mapped it to, for a SPECIFIC upload.

    Usage:
        <AntibioticNameDisplay Abbreviation="@antibiotic" ResolvedFullName="@resolved" />

    The component is presentational: it does not query. The caller resolves every
    name on the page once, with
    AntibioticAbbreviationService.GetDisplayNameLookupAsync, and passes the result
    down. A component that queried per instance would issue one query per rendered
    name against the scoped DbContext, and EF Core throws when a second operation
    starts on a context whose first operation has not finished.

    THREE outcomes are possible, and the third is the one that matters:

      - The name is already complete ("Amoxicillin"). It is rendered as-is with
        NO marker, because nothing is missing. Marking it "unmapped" would tell a
        reader that a decision is outstanding when the file has already given the
        answer.
      - The name is an abbreviation ("AMK %S") and a mapping exists. The meaning
        is shown beside it.
      - The name is an abbreviation and no mapping exists. It is shown with a
        muted "unmapped" marker, because a decision genuinely is outstanding.
*@

@if (IsCompleteName)
{
    <span class="antibiotic-name">
        <span class="antibiotic-name__abbreviation">@Abbreviation</span>
    </span>
}
else if (ResolvedFullName is null)
{
    <span class="antibiotic-name antibiotic-name--unmapped">
        <span class="antibiotic-name__abbreviation">@Abbreviation</span>
        <span class="antibiotic-name__marker" title="@Localizer["AntibioticName_UnmappedTooltip"]">
            @Localizer["AntibioticName_Unmapped"]
        </span>
    </span>
}
else
{
    <span class="antibiotic-name">
        <span class="antibiotic-name__abbreviation">@Abbreviation</span>
        <span class="antibiotic-name__full-name">(@ResolvedFullName)</span>
    </span>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The abbreviation string exactly as it appears in the spreadsheet header.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Abbreviation { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The full name this abbreviation maps to, or null when it is unmapped.
    /// Resolved by the caller, so rendering many names costs one query rather
    /// than one per component.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ResolvedFullName { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the name is a complete antibiotic name rather than an
    /// abbreviation, so no mapping applies to it.
    /// </summary>
    private bool IsCompleteName => !AntibioticNameClassifier.IsAbbreviation(Abbreviation);
}
